config DRM_AXIADO
        bool "HDMI specific extensions"
        depends on DRM && OF
        select DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION
        select DRM_KMS_HELPER
        select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
        help
          Choose this option to enable support for the Axiado SoC
          Display Subsystem DRM driver.

          The Axiado SoC integrates a display pipeline consisting of
          multiple hardware blocks connected via the standard
          device-tree ports/endpoint graph bindings, including a
          display controller, HDMI transmitter, and associated
          clock and PHY resources.

          This driver supports the SoC's integrated HDMI output as
          well as display controllers exposed through the
          display-subsystem container node, providing KMS/DRM
          support for video output on Axiado-based platforms.

          If you want to use the Axiado SoC integrated HDMI or
          related display controllers under the Direct Rendering
          Manager (DRM) framework, say Y or M here.

          If unsure, say N.

if DRM_AXIADO

config AXIADO_LCDC
	bool "Axiado DB9000 LCD controller (LCDC)"
	default y
	help
	  Enable the Digital Blocks DB9000 LCD controller sub-driver. It
	  provides the CRTC and primary plane of the Axiado display
	  subsystem and binds as a component of the display-subsystem
	  master.

	  If unsure, say Y.

endif # DRM_AXIADO
